---
title: Pistachio Inside-Outside Cake
author: Cheryl Spinner
---

== Cake ==

Preheat #oven{} to 350°F.

Combine @cake mix{1%pkg}(white or yellow), @pistachio pudding mix{1%pkg}, @eggs{3}, @club soda{1%cup}, and @vegtable oil{1%cup}. Optionally, add @?nuts{1/2%cup}(chopped).

Beat with a mixer on medium speed for ~{2%minutes}.

Pour batter into a greased and floured #Bundt pan{}.

Bake for ~{50%minutes}, or until done.

Cool in the pan for ~{15%minutes}, then invert onto a #cooling rack{} and let cool completely.

Slice the cake horizontally into three layers. Spread 1/2 cup frosting between each layer, then fill the center with the remaining frosting.

Refrigerate for ~{2%hours}.

== Frosting ==

Whip together @milk{1 1/2%cups}(cold), @Dream Whip{1%envelope}, and @pistachio pudding mix{1%pkg} until thickened, about ~{5%minutes}.